WEBVTT

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:16.500
Question: What problems arise from a lack of airtightness?

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Problems caused by a lack of airtightness include:
air infiltration into the building.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Air can also leave the building (exfiltration).

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.000
The answer also claims poorer indoor air quality, higher energy use,
and health problems for occupants.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:05.000
PDF page 91: Inadequate airtightness loses conditioned indoor air
and consequently increases a building's energy use.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:22.000
